{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Handling Exceptions in Java: Try and Catch  "}, {"type": "position", "content": 12}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear and use to talk about handling exceptions in Java."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand important information about client software for the identity metasystem in spoken or written documents."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.  Exchanges simple information on principles, concepts, and features of general purpose computer programming languages."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe7n5le02ob12re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Present Perfect vs. Simple Past"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<strong>Present perfect tense</strong> and <strong>simple past</strong> tense are both used for talking about the past, but there are big differences between them. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I've not read anything extensive about it, but yesterday a friend told me that there is something called exceptions."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I thought  that those errors were not able to be spotted."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I've talked with all programmers in the faculty and that's new for me."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read the following sentences:<br><br>  <i>I <b>have had problems</b> when creating references to some objects. (1)<br> Last month, I <b>learned how to use the garbage collection in Java. </b>  (2)</i><br><br>  On one hand, the first example is an affirmative sentence in present perfect. As you can see, this first example is talking about an event in the past but it is closely related to the events in the present. On the other hand, the second sentence is written in simple past tense, which is used to talk about events that started in the past and finished in the past, which is why we usually use a time expression. <br><br>  You can use both tenses together to narrate an event:<br><br>  <i>I <b>haven't read about java</b> (1) since we <b>started</b> the semester (2).</i><br><br>  Look at the following chart to understand the grammatical structures for each tense:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":9,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present perfect tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Simple past tense\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Affirmative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Subject + Auxiliary verb have in present (have or has)+ <br>verb in past participle +  Complement.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Subject + Verb in past (regular or irregular) + Complement.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example:<br> I <strong>have read</strong> that article twice.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example: I <strong>read</strong> the article last night.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Negative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Subject + Auxiliary verb in negative (haven't or hasn't) + <br>verb in past participle + Complement.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Subject + Auxiliary verb did in negative (did not or didn't) + Verb in present + Complement.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example:  I <strong>haven't done</strong> my assignment yet.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example:  I <strong>didn't do</strong> my homework.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Yes/No Questions\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Auxiliary verb (have or has) + Subject<br> + Verb in past participle + Complement + Question mark (?)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Auxiliary verb (did) + Subject <br>+ Verb in present + Complement + Question mark (?)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example: <strong> Have </strong>you <strong>gone </strong>to the lake?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example: <strong>Did </strong>you <strong>go</strong> to the lake?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Wh Questions\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Interrogative adverb (what, where, when, etc.) + Auxiliary verb (have or has) <br>+ Subject + Verb in past participle + Complement + Question mark (?)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Interrogative adverb (what, where, when, etc.) + Auxiliary verb (did) <br>+ Subject + Verb in present + Complement + Question mark (?)\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example: What <strong>have </strong>you <strong>done </strong>lately?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Example: What <strong>did </strong>you <strong>do</strong> yesterday?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Quantifiers"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<strong>Quantifiers</strong> are words used in measurement to express a quantity or amount. These words are used with countable and uncountable nouns. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "We've been reading a lot of texts on programming."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I've talked with all programmers in the faculty and that's new for me."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Catch blocks can save programmers a great deal of time."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In the following chart, you'll find some <strong>quantifiers</strong> classified. Be careful, you have to think if the noun you're going to describe is countable or uncountable. "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Countable nouns\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Uncountable nouns\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Both\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A majority of\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A bit\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"All\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Many\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Much\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A lot of/Lots of\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A few/Few\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A little/Little\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Plenty of\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Several\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A great deal of\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Some\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A great number of\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"A large quantity of / A large amount of \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"An\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "How to Write a Summary"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "A <strong>summary</strong> is a tool that comes in handy when you want to fully understand a text, because it's a way of restating what the author wanted to say. Here are some tips for writing a good summary. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<strong>1.</strong> Read carefully the text you are going to summarize."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<strong>2.</strong> If it's possible, take notes and try to understand how the text was written. You can ask yourself the following questions: What's the function of this paragraph, what kind of paragraph is it? How is it connected with the other ideas in the text?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<strong>3.</strong> Look for the main ideas of the text because in a summary, secondary information is not needed. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<strong>4.</strong> As writing is a perfectible process, it's a good idea to make a draft first."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<strong>5.</strong> If you are going to quote or paraphrase something, don't forget to mention the author and the original source of the text. In the summary, it's preferable to use the author's last name."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<strong>6.</strong> Be precise and keep it short, your summary cannot be longer than the original text. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "hinder from "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to prevent something from happening "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb): "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: An exception is a situation in which a code error hinders the program from performing well.  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n5le02ob12aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "see the error of your ways "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be aware of what you're doing wrong.  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression): "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Java happens to see the error of its ways."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n5le02ob12aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "foretell "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to predict "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb): "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You can foretell an error using a try block in which you write the code you need."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n5le02ob12aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "spot"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to identify or detect "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb): "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: What do you know about spotting errors in Java?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n5le02ob12aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "cross out "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to delete "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb): "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: How can I cross out the catch block?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n5le02ob12aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about exceptions in Java."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Take notes about the information you are reading."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a report to explain what an exception is and how to handle it."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your paragraph with your partners. "}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I search information about exceptions in Java. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write a report to explain the concept of exception in java and the way to handle it."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share with my partners. "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "lab